VLA models. VLA models are a class of models that unify multi-modal understanding and action generation for robotic control (Physical Intelligence et al., 2025; NVIDIA et al., 2025). Typically, VLA models are initialized from VLMs pretrained on large-scale image-text corpora, and then finetuned on robotics dataset containing expert trajectories: D = {τj}M
